{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014MepBnLAHcGTpByDXnwD21","type":"tool_result","content":"60:merged, and with them the meaning of three governance checks: the VETO\n143:  agent-frontmatter VETO validator, the Codex pin file, the framework's own\n150:- **The VETO floor moved from a closed list to family patterns.**\n151:  - Before, an agent file with `veto_floor: true` had to declare one of\n154:    id that matches the families in `_lib/model_currency.py`: Claude Opus\n168:  - Now all three call `is_allowed_model` in `_lib/model_currency.py`\n225:  canonical only as well: `_lib/model_currency.py`, the VETO-floor\n227:  `escalation_signals.py` now call as part of their VETO-floor check; and\n385:- **The VETO floor admits retired ids** (Security and governance, above).\n483:- The VETO floor now admits retired model ids. If your veto roles must not\n668:  `tier_a_model_currency`, that is never red. Installs do not receive\n698:  the model that served each call with the declared one, VETO floor\n1047:allowlist and the VETO floor. New installs ship at `xhigh` effort; an\n1064:### Changed — Claude Opus 5.5 is the session default and joins the VETO floor (PLAN-193, ADR-149 Amendment 3)\n1073:- **VETO floor.** `claude-opus-5-5` joins the ids an agent file with\n1074:  `veto_floor: true` may declare (the ADR-149 block and\n1075:  `agent_frontmatter.VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`, kept equal by test). That makes it\n1076:  ELIGIBLE; it moves no agent: every shipped VETO-bearing agent file keeps\n1368:  ignored — a VETO rite can fall below its floor tier. A test now asserts\n2002:  deliberately never automatic: the VETO floor, the pins and the agent\n2006:### Fixed — seven VETO-bearing skills were demoted to name-only (`b7dad83`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91f7b0d1-4b6c-452f-a17c-4e8edc70c372","uuid":"cb94dc0b-bcdd-4061-9750-84f58198fe56","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:46:17.616Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filen