{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V2QH1CWKEQzoSnenBMcNGb","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t-# PLAN-094-FOLLOWUP Wave A.3-fail-open (option B) — module-level durability\n301\t-# indicator for the last `spool_append()` call. audit_emit wire-in checks\n302\t-# `last_append_succeeded()` after each call; on False, falls through to the\n303\t-# sync canonical write path. Preserves the existing fail-open invariant\n304\t-# (`spool_append` never raises to caller) while restoring durability defense\n305\t-# depth on per-PID spool flock alloc / encode / OSError / unexpected paths.\n306\t _LAST_APPEND_SUCCEEDED = True\n307\t-\n308\t-\n309\t def last_append_succeeded() -> bool:\n310\t-    \"\"\"Return True if the most recent spool_append() persisted durably.\n311\t-\n312\t-    audit_emit wire-in uses this to decide whether to fall back to the\n313\t-    sync canonical write path (False = silent-drop on spool side; sync\n314\t-    is now responsible for durability of THIS event).\n315\t-    \"\"\"\n316\t+    \"\"\"Whether the last spool_append persisted durably.\"\"\"\n317\t     return _LAST_APPEND_SUCCEEDED\n318\t \n319\t-# P1-2 journal buffer state (per-PID amortized fsync).\n320\t-# Buffer envelopes in memory; flush + fsync at: drain boundary, signal,\n321\t-# atexit, or every _JOURNAL_FLUSH_EVERY writes. ADR-055-AMEND-1 §3 line 96:\n322\t-# \"journal fsync every 100ms OR 10 emits\".\n323\t+# Per-PID journal buffer; flush at drain boundaries or every ten writes.\n324\t _JOURNAL_FLUSH_EVERY = 10\n325\t@@ -684,4 +551,2 @@ def set_forensic_emitter(emit_fn: Callable[[str, Dict[str, Any]], None]) -> None\n326\t     _FORENSIC_EMIT = emit_fn\n327\t-\n328\t-\n329\t def _forensic(action: str, fields: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n330\t@@ -706,9 +571,2 @@ def _forensic(action: str, fields: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n331\t         _IN_FORENSIC_EMIT = False\n332\t-\n333\t-\n334\t-# -------------------------------------------------------------------