en, concurrent-write safe, redaction, stdlib-only) were removed and now appear nowhere in the facade. Minimal fix: restore a short version of the docstring.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-12.verdict.txt:14:- reality-ledger: the facade supplies _REPO_ROOT and redact_secrets, and constants.__all__ exports the underscore names that findings/walking take via star-import.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-05.verdict.txt:26:   - ceo-boot.py:120 redefines check_tier_a_spec_version_drift after TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py:376) has already bound the copy at model_persona.py:6, so the facade copy is dead for the registry.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-27.verdict.txt:20:Validation used read-only inspection and in-memory checks. Boot marker/audit ordering passed. Full registry coverage verification was limited by a redaction placeholder that makes one copied module unparseable; that artifact is not reported as a release defect.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-29.verdict.txt:35:2. P2 — .claude/scripts/_contamination_inventory.py:76-81 and :89. For an index entry with mode 120000, _blob only calls os.readlink.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-18.verdict.txt:1:No P0 or false declared condition found in payload 18. Benign Python 3.9 checks passed for original-text offsets, overlapping redactions, extracted imports, facade globals and policy exports.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-26.verdict.txt:27:P2-2 — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120-178 (a second copy of check_tier_a_spec_version_drift)\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-26.verdict.txt:28:- Failure: TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py:376) binds the copy at model_persona.py:6, because the registry is built inside install(), before the facade redefines the name at :120. The facade copy is never dispatched.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-23.verdict.txt:14:- _precompact_parts.install exec's each part into the facade's nam