{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch77QhLpZYwxM3mvRgZXC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SGCaMSKLDd7CVhUBwF7fUF","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"SCOPE OF PAYLOAD 14/34\n- New files: _lib/_spool_writer_parts/writer.py; _lib/agent_spawn/{__init__,advisories,entrypoint,file_assignment,model_routing,outcome_telemetry,prompt_rules,skill_reference}.py.\n- Modified: _lib/agent_frontmatter.py (the VETO-floor predicate).\n- Also read: the facades (spool_writer.py, check_agent_spawn.py), the binders (_spool_writer_parts/__init__.py, _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py, agent_spawn/__init__.py), model_currency.py, the kernel list, CHANGELOG [1.4.4], model-deprecations.json, redact.py, scripts/install.sh with _framework_manifest_set.sh, and _python-hook.sh.\n- Base text for comparison: the removed lines of the base check_agent_spawn.py and spool_writer.py in the committed rc evidence (.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/diff-rc1-20.patch and diff-rc1-19.patch).\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS THIS PAYLOAD TOUCHES (all TRUE against the code)\n- Condition 5: check_arbitration_kernel.py:310 has \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\" and :332 has \"_lib/model_currency.py\". agent_frontmatter.py is a kernel path (:198). spool_writer.py has never been a kernel path, so leaving _spool_writer_parts/ off the list loses no kernel coverage.\n- Condition 7: check_agent_spawn.py and spool_writer.py are thin facades. Their logic now lives in the part modules, so a hand patch must be re-applied there. agent_spawn/ is a kernel path.\n- Condition 8: _python-hook.sh:410 still exports CEO_HOOK_BOUNDED_EXIT=1.\n- Condition 9:\n  - What the code does: agent_frontmatter.py:256-261 admits model_currency.is_veto_floor_model(actual) OR membership in VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED. The family regex is model_currency.py:16; _RETIRED holds only \"claude-opus-4-1\".\n  - Retired ids pass: model-deprecations.json lists claude-opus-4-0 (retired 2026-06-15) and claude-opus-4-6-fast / claude-opus-4-7-fast (retired). All three match _FLOOR, so they pass the floor, as condition 9 says.\n  - CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 150-163 state this honestly, naming gpt-5-mini, o3-mini and o4-mini and the stale docstring.\n  - The expected_model path is still exact equality, so it is unchanged.\n\nMOVED-CODE VERIFICATION (no defect found)\n- writer.py: line for line the same as the base spool_writer.py text (diff-rc1-19.patch:344-702), including the deferred header fsync (sync_header=False), which predates this delta. The only addition is a QDSAA-FUNCAO-LONGA comment.\n  - Every free name it uses is defined in the facade (spool_writer.py), e.g. _SPOOL_HEADER_CACHE, _ORDINAL_COUNTER, _spool_path, _breadcrumb, _JOURNAL_BUFFER, FileLock and SPOOL_LOCK_TIMEOUT.\n  - _spool_writer_parts.install rebinds each function onto the facade's globals, so `global _IN_SPOOL_APPEND, _LAST_APPEND_SUCCEEDED` writes to the facade.\n  - __all__ exports only functions, so nothing overwrites a facade value.\n- agent_spawn: I compared the security-relevant blocks with the base text and found them identical:\n  - the FILE ASSIGNMENT grammar (regexes, _fa_* helpers, _classify_file_assignment), _recent_file_assignments and _enforce_spawn_rails;\n  - _skill_ref_resolve_path, _enforce_spec_context_unicode / _unicode_hardblock_enforced and _validate_spawn_prompt_has_no_secrets;\n  - _BLOCK_REASON_MARKERS and main(). main() only gains the _SPAWN_COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR allow path.\n- Binding: model_routing, advisories, prompt_rules, outcome_telemetry and entrypoint go through _audit_emit_parts.install(package=\"_lib.agent_spawn\"), which deep-copies mutable values and rebinds functions to the hook's globals. skill_reference and file_assignment go through bind(). No two parts' __all__ share a name, and none collides with a facade name. Every free name resolves at call time.\n- outcome_telemetry._audit_log_path still reaches the real writer path, because audit_emit exports _log_path (_audit_emit_parts/writer.py:187).\n- skill_reference still sees real replacement tokens: redact.py still emits [JWT], [API_KEY] and the rest, independently of secret_patterns.py.\n- Python and stdlib: standard library only, Python 3.9-safe. Annotations are lazy under `from __future__`, and there is no 3.10+ syntax.\n- Delivery: install_lib_selective (install.sh:1520-1550) globs every top-level _lib entry, and _framework_path_excluded excludes neither new package, so a fresh install delivers both.\n- sys.path side effect: the parts insert .claude/hooks/_lib at sys.path[0]. No _lib module or subpackage name collides with a Python 3.9 stdlib module or with a .claude/scripts module today.\n\nFAIL DIRECTION\n- A component load failure under __main__ prints {} (allow) and exits 0, and main() allows on a bind failure. That is fail-open on an infrastructure fault.\n- The input-side fail-closed checks (skill-reference sub-checks, invisible-unicode hardblock when armed, prompt-defense gate) are unchanged.\n- The new code adds no write site and no symlink path.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nCARRIED, ALREADY DECLARED (signed lane notes claude-p12 / claude-p19), STILL TRUE AGAINST THIS CODE\n- P1, agent_spawn/file_assignment.py:327-380 with _python-hook.sh:410: _recent_file_assignments tails only the canonical audit log, but under the bounded exit a hook's spawn_file_assignment_recorded row stays in its per-PID spool. With CEO_SPAWN_OVERLAP_GUARD=1, a second spawn that claims the same path is therefore allowed. The miss is fail-open and blocks no legitimate session.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. (new) agent_frontmatter.py:79-82\n   - Problem: the same faulty predicate module gives opposite results depending on how it fails. The import catches only ImportError. If model_currency.py is missing, the floor falls back to the closed set (stricter). If it is present but unimportable, for example a half-written file raising SyntaxError, the error escapes agent_frontmatter. check_agent_spawn.py:68-71 then sets _agent_frontmatter=None and skips the whole VETO-floor check. Unguarded importers crash instead.\n   - Fix: catch Exception and fall back to the closed set, then cover both faults with a test.\n2. (new, cosmetic) agent_frontmatter.py:139-144: the provenance comments for claude-opus-5 (ADR-181) and claude-opus-5-5 (ADR-149 Amendment 3) were deleted in the same diff that widened the floor. That runs against the module's own aim at :96-101 that floor edits stay \"forensically visible in diffs\". The docstrings at :22-28 and :208-212 still say \"∈ VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED\". The CHANGELOG declares that staleness; the block text at check_agent_spawn.py:312-316, \"set membership, not one id\", is the carried rc P2. Fix: restore the comments and update the docstrings and the block text to name the family predicate.\n3. (carried from claude-rc1-13, pre-existing; redact.py is unchanged in the delta) agent_spawn/skill_reference.py:250-251: sub-check 11 calls redact_secrets(text) with the default max_chars=120. The token test therefore sees only about the first 117 characters, roughly the frontmatter, and a secret in the body of a referenced SKILL.md is never flagged. Fix: call it with max_chars=0, chunked over the 64 KiB input cap.\n4. (carried rc P2-1) _spool_writer_parts/writer.py:29-31 and :52-63:\n   - _HOOKS_DIR resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib and is inserted at sys.path[0].\n   - The part also defines its own constants (K_MAX, SPOOL_LOCK_TIMEOUT and others), which the bound functions never read; editing them silently has no effect.\n   - There is no collision today, so the risk is latent.\n   - Fix: drop the sys.path block and the constants from the part.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Payload 14 makes none of the declared conditions it touches (5, 7, 8, 9) false: writer.py and the security-relevant agent_spawn blocks match the base text line for line, bind to their facades with fail-open infrastructure handling, ship to fresh installs and stay standard-library only and Python 3.9 compatible; the VETO-floor widening is honestly declared, there is no P0 and no new P1, and the one live P1 here is already declared in the signed lane notes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":230181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91f7b0d1-4b6c-452f-a17c-4e8edc70c372","uuid":"7c7a0608-64f3-4435-bf52-1ef29f6037fd","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:52:26.498Z","request_id":"req_011Ch77Qh7fsAsidD5g2yR8T","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SGCaMSKLDd7CVhUBwF7fUF":{"report":"SCOPE OF PAYLOAD 14/34\n- New files: _lib/_spool_writer_parts/writer.py; _lib/agent_spawn/{__init__,advisories,entrypoint,file_assignment,model_routing,outcome_telemetry,prompt_rules,skill_reference}.py.\n- Modified: _lib/agent_frontmatter.py (the VETO-floor predicate).\n- Also read: the facades (spool_writer.py, check_agent_spawn.py), the binders (_spool_writer_parts/__init__.py, _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py, agent_spawn/__init__.py), model_currency.py, the kernel list, CHANGELOG [1.4.4], model-deprecations.json, redact.py, scripts/install.sh with _framework_manifest_set.sh, and _python-hook.sh.\n- Base text for comparison: the removed lines of the base check_agent_spawn.py and spool_writer.py in the committed rc evidence (.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/diff-rc1-20.patch and diff-rc1-19.patch).\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS THIS PAYLOAD TOUCHES (all TRUE against the code)\n- Condition 5: check_arbitration_kernel.py:310 has \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\" and :332 has \"_lib/model_currency.py\". agent_frontmatter.py is a kernel path 