with _python-hook.sh:410: _recent_file_assignments tails only the canonical audit log, but under the bounded exit a hook's spawn_file_assignment_recorded row stays in its per-PID spool. With CEO_SPAWN_OVERLAP_GUARD=1, a second spawn that claims the same path is therefore allowed. The miss is fail-open and blocks no legitimate session.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. (new) agent_frontmatter.py:79-82\n   - Problem: the same faulty predicate module gives opposite results depending on how it fails. The import catches only ImportError. If model_currency.py is missing, the floor falls back to the closed set (stricter). If it is present but unimportable, for example a half-written file raising SyntaxError, the error escapes agent_frontmatter. check_agent_spawn.py:68-71 then sets _agent_frontmatter=None and skips the whole VETO-floor check. Unguarded importers crash instead.\n   - Fix: catch Exception and fall back to the closed set, then cover both faults with a test.\n2. (new, cosmetic) agent_frontmatter.py:139-144: the provenance comments for claude-opus-5 (ADR-181) and claude-opus-5-5 (ADR-149 Amendment 3) were deleted in the same diff that widened the floor. That runs against the module's own aim at :96-101 that floor edits stay \"forensically visible in diffs\". The docstrings at :22-28 and :208-212 still say \"∈ VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED\". The CHANGELOG declares that staleness; the block text at check_agent_spawn.py:312-316, \"set membership, not one id\", is the carried rc P2. Fix: restore the comments and update the docstrings and the block text to name the family predicate.\n3. (carried from claude-rc1-13, pre-existing; redact.py is unchanged in the delta) agent_spawn/skill_reference.py:250-251: sub-check 11 calls redact_secrets(text) with the default max_chars=120. The token test therefore sees only about the first 117 characters, roughly the frontmatter, and a secret in the body of a referenced SKILL.md is never flagged. Fix: call it with max_chars=0, chunked over the 64 KiB input cap.\n4. (carried rc P2-1) _spool_writer_parts/writer.py:29-31 and :52-63:\n   - _HOOKS_DIR resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib and is inserted at sys.path[0].\n   - The part also defines its own constants (K_MAX, SPOOL_LOCK_TIMEOUT and others), which the bound functions never read; editing them silently has no effect.\n   - There is no collision today, so the risk is latent.\n   - Fix: drop the sys.path block and the constants from the part.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Payload 14 makes none of the declared conditions it touches (5, 7, 8, 9) false: writer.py and the security-relevant agent_spawn blocks match the base text line for line, bind to their facades with fail-open infrastructure handling, ship to fresh installs and stay standard-library only and Python 3.9 compatible; the VETO-floor widening is honestly declared, there is no P0 and no new P1, and the one live P1 here is already declared in the signed lane notes."}}}
